      "item": "cold water",
      "quantity": 0.25,
      "unit": "cup"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Warm the olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and cook briefly until fragrant, then transfer it to a slow cooker."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Add the onion, soy sauce, salt, ground black pepper, and white sugar to the slow cooker. Stir in the beef sirloin."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Cover and cook on low for 8 hours, until the beef is tender and reaches at least 145°F on a food thermometer. Let whole-cut beef rest for 3 minutes before serving.",
      "timer_minutes": 480
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Stir in the ground black pepper and green bell peppers."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Mix the cornstarch with the cold water until smooth. Stir the mixture into the cooker and continue cooking until the sauce is thickened, adding the soy sauce as directed by the cooker’s sauce mixture."
    }
  ],
